n in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.play:url-emitter_state_function)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:particlefx.play","jsName":"play","line":77,"member":"play","modulePath":["particlefx"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the particle fx that should start playing.","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"optional callback function that will be called when an emitter attached to this particlefx changes state.","optional":true,"rawName":"emitter_state_function","rawType":"fun(self:script_instance, id:hash, emitter:hash, state:particlefx.EMITTER_STATE)"}],"rawName":"particlefx.play","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"Resets a shader constant for a particle FX component emitter.\nThe constant must be defined in the material assigned to the emitter.\nResetting a constant through this function implies that the value defined in the material will be used.\nWhich particle FX to reset a constant for is identified by the URL.\n\n**Examples:**\n\nThe following examples assumes that the particle FX has id \"particlefx\", it\ncontains an emitter with the id \"emitter\" and that the default-material in builtins is used, which defines the constant \"tint\".\nIf you assign a custom material to the sprite, you can reset the constants defined there in the same manner.\n\nHow to reset the tinting of particles from an emitter:\n\n```lua\nfunction init(self)\n    particlefx.reset_constant(\"#particlefx\", \"emitter\", \"tint\")\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.reset_constant:url-emitter-constant)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:particlefx.reset_constant","jsName":"resetConstant","line":102,"member":"reset_constant","modulePath":["particlefx"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the particle FX that should have a constant reset","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"the id of the emitter","optional":false,"rawName":"emitter","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"the name of the constant","optional":false,"rawName":"constant","rawType":"string|hash"}],"rawName":"particlefx.reset_constant","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"Sets a shader constant for a particle FX component emitter.\nThe constant must be defined in the material assigned to the emitter.\nSetting a constant through this function will override the value set for that constant in the material.\nThe value will be overridden until particlefx.reset_constant is called.\nWhich particle FX to set a constant for is identified by the URL.\n\n**Examples:**\n\nThe following examples assumes that the particle FX has id \"particlefx\", it\ncontains an emitter with the id \"emitter\" and that the default-material in builtins is used, which defines the constant \"tint\".\nIf you assign a custom material to the sprite, you can reset the constants defined there in the same manner.\n\nHow to tint particles from an emitter red:\n\n```lua\nfunction init(self)\n    particlefx.set_constant(\"#particlefx\", \"emitter\", \"tint\", vmath.vector4(1, 0, 0, 1))\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.set_constant:url-emitter-constant-value)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:particlefx.set_constant","jsName":"setConstant","line":129,"member":"set_constant","modulePath":["particlefx"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the particle FX that should have a constant set","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"the id of the emitter","optional":false,"rawName":"emitter","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"the name of the constant","optional":false,"rawName":"constant","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"the value of the constant","optional":false,"rawName":"value","rawType":"vector4"}],"rawName":"particlefx.set_constant","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"Stops a particle FX component from playing.\nStopping a particle FX does not remove already spawned particles.\nWhich particle FX to stop is identified by the URL.\n\n**Examples:**\n\nHow to stop a particle fx when a game object is deleted and immediately also clear\nany spawned particles:\n\n```lua\nfunction final(self)\n    particlefx.stop(\"#particlefx\", { clear = true })\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.stop:url-options)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:particlefx.stop","jsName":"stop","line":149,"member":"stop","modulePath":["particlefx"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the particle fx that should stop playing","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"options used when stopping the particle fx","optional":true,"rawName":"options","rawType":"particlefx.stop_options"}],"rawName":"particlefx.stop","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"}],"types":[{"description":"","disposition":"generated-type","fields":[{"description":"Functions and properties for controlling particle effect component playback and\nshader constants.\npostspawn state The emitter is not spawning any particles, but has particles that are still alive.\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.EMITTER_STATE)","line":18,"optional":false,"rawName":"EMITTER_STATE_POSTSPAWN","rawType":"particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"prespawn state The emitter will be in this state when it has been started but before spawning any particles. Normally the emitter is in this state for a short time, depending on if a start delay has been set for this emitter or not.\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.EMITTER_STATE)","line":22,"optional":false,"rawName":"EMITTER_STATE_PRESPAWN","rawType":"particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"sleeping state The emitter does not have any living particles and will not spawn any particles in this state.\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.EMITTER_STATE)","line":26,"optional":false,"rawName":"EMITTER_STATE_SLEEPING","rawType":"particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"spawning state The emitter is spawning particles.\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.EMITTER_STATE)","line":30,"optional":false,"rawName":"EMITTER_STATE_SPAWNING","rawType":"particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"}],"kind":"class","line":12,"name":"defold_api.particlefx","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"","disposition":"generated-type","kind":"enum","line":33,"name":"defold_enum.particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","rawType":"integer","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"Emitter states\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.EMITTER_STATE)","disposition":"generated-type","kind":"alias","line":44,"name":"particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","rawType":"defold_enum.particlefx.EMITTER_STATE","source":"doc/particlefx.lua"},{"description":"","disposition":"generated-type","fields":[{"description":"Options used when stopping particle effects.\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/particlefx-lua#particlefx.stop_options)\nInstantly clear spawned particles.","line":1450,"optional":true,"rawName":"clear","rawType":"boolean","source":"doc/meta.lua"}],"kind":"class","line":1446,"name":"particlefx.stop_options","source":"doc/meta.lua"}]}}